## Objective
- Act as an autonomous bug-bounty agent per `skills/AGENT.md`, testing all 85 top-level routes of `https://console.byteplus.com` from `data/targets.txt` for client-side then server-side vulnerabilities.
- Record only confirmed, reproducible findings in `result/`; currently no confirmed vulnerability.

## Important Details
- Repo root / cwd: `/home/runner/work/aaii-aautomattionn/aaii-aautomattionn`.
- Scope: only URLs in `data/targets.txt` (`https://console.byteplus.com/...` routes) plus same-origin JS/API needed to exercise them. No subdomains/siblings/third parties/CDNs.
- Explicitly out of scope: `arkbff-ap-southeast1.console.byteplus.com`, `modelark-api.console.byteplus.com`, `res.gcloudcache.com`, other sibling domains.
- Must read `skills/AGENT.md` fully; also `skills/client-side-skill.md`, `skills/server-side-skill.md`. No user questions — self-answer and act.
- Testing constraints: use only test-owned/disposable data; avoid real-user data; avoid billable resource creation; clean up created objects.
- Test accounts (`creds/test-account.txt`, intentionally public):
  - A: `adoringjepsen1@fearlessmails.com` / `Acd3423@#345566`; AccountId `3000823185`; root identity `test-user-123`.
  - B: `testt456` / `Acd3423@#345`; root AccountId `3001021825`.
  - B also has IAM user `admin12345` (UserId `87449062`, `AdministratorAccess`), password same as B root, login via IAM form with main account `testt456`.
- B IAM users: `testtttt` (Id `97235517`), `admin12345` (Id `87449062`, admin).
- IAM console API: `POST https://console.byteplus.com/api/v2/batch/iam` with JSON `{Actions:[{Service:"iam",Action,...,Version:"2018-01-01",Region:"ap-southeast-1",Method:"GET|POST",Query:"...",ContentType:"application/x-www-form-urlencoded"}]}`.
- Auth material for curl: `/tmp/cookies.json`, `/tmp/cookiehdr.txt`; CSRF token from cookie `csrfToken`.
- Environment: Chrome 156 headless at `http://127.0.0.1:9222`; chrome-devtools MCP works; `rg` is NOT installed — use Python/grep. Node `v22.23.4`, `curl`, `python3`, `opencode` available.
- Session start UTC `2026-10-29T06:25:00Z`; conversation progressed to ~`06:50Z`; testing window ~5h35m, hard timeout ~5h55m.
- No confirmed vulnerability yet; `result/confirmed-vuln.txt` remains header-only.

## Work State
### Completed
- Preflight and prior crawl work completed:
  - Fetched all 85 route HTMLs → `/tmp/bp/pages/*.html`, all HTTP 200.
  - Crawled all 85 routes with `tools/crawl.mjs` → `/tmp/bp/crawl.json`; 2324 unique scripts, 276 unique API URLs.
  - Downloaded JS bundles to `/tmp/bp/js` (2217 files, ~738MB).
  - Static-analysis dumps: `/tmp/bp/loc_candidates.txt`, `decode_loc.txt`, `param_nav.txt`, `source_sink.txt`, `scan_sink.txt`, `msgscan.txt`, `msg_app.txt`.
- Account/profile API discovery:
  - `/api/top/account_verify/ap-southeast-1/2018-01-01/{GetProfileInfo,GetRawProfileInfo,UpdateProfile,CompleteProfile,SupplementProfileInfo,SendProfileSMSCaptcha,SendProfileVoiceCaptcha,CreateGoChinaApplication}`.
  - `UpdateProfile` / `CompleteProfile` payloads include `Tel`, `IdentityType` (`individual`→1, `enterprise`→2), `CountryCode`, form fields; call sites in `js/94e591e322478cc8.js`, `js/b441167ead1eb44e.js`, `js/fa1839aa81669f86.js`.
  - `GetProfileInfo` as A returns masked PII (`VerifyName "t*******"`, `FullName "t***"`, `Tel "+319********48"`, `Status:1`, `IdentityType:2`).
  - `GetRawProfileInfo` as A returns unmasked own-account data (`VerifyName "test-org"`, `FullName "test"`, `Tel "+3197058047048"`), but unauthenticated request fails with `InvalidCSRFToken`. No vulnerability established.
- Open-redirect tests:
  - Fresh A login with `?redirectURI=https%3A%2F%2Fexample.com%2F` ended at `/home`; ignored.
  - `redirectURI=//example.com/` login ended at `/home`; ignored.
  - `redirectURI=javascript:document.title='PWN'` returned Chrome error page / HTTP 403 “Access to console.byteplus.com was denied” (WAF block).
- SSRF tests against `/api/v2/batch/iam`:
  - `Service:"ecs"` + `DescribeInstances` works (0 instances).
  - `Service:"http://169.254.169.254"` → HTTP 404 `RequestNotFound`.
  - `Service:"file:///etc/passwd"` → HTTP 404 `RequestNotFound`.
  - `Action:"../ecs/DescribeInstances"` invalid. No SSRF.
- Cross-tenant / IDOR tests:
  - B `ListUsers` with `AccountId=3000823185` still returns B’s users; `AccountId` ignored.
  - B `GetUser` for A’s IAM user `bb-dts-pm-mtbovts1-c46806` returns `UserNotExist` with/without `AccountId`.
  - DataRangers: B org id `84`, A org id `2100230837`; B requests to A’s org `/datarangers/api/org/2100230837/app/list` and `/user/get` returned `{"code":400,"message":"用户不存在或者不属于该组织"}` after supplying required `x-csrf-token` + `x-caller: portal`. No IDOR.
  - A DataRangers org is “Demo体验” with demo apps; Add Project disabled. Demo/shared data likely.
  - Ark `ListApiKeys` from B with `AccountId` body or `X-Ark-Meta-Account-Id: 3000823185` header returned B-scoped `TotalCount:0`; header ignored.
  - Legacy `/api/iam/account?...` and `/api/iam/project?...` with `X-Account-Id` returned HTTP 404 on console origin; wrong endpoint.
- CORS test:
  - `Origin: https://evil.example` on `ListApiKeys` and `GetProfileInfo` returned static `access-control-allow-origin: http://console.byteplus.com` + `access-control-allow-credentials: true`; not reflected.
  - `/api/v2/batch/iam` and `/signin/status/identity` returned no CORS headers. No CORS vuln.
- IAM mass-assignment / write tests:
  - B root `CreateUser` `zzagenttest56334014` with `AccountId=3000823185` created the user in B (`AccountId:3001021825`); `AccountId` ignored.
  - Attempted `UpdateUser` with `DisplayName`/`Description` then correct `NewDisplayName`/`NewDescription`; got HTTP 403 with empty `text/plain` body for both B root and `admin12345`.
  - Deleted `zzagenttest56334014` via `DeleteUser` GET → HTTP 200 success. Cleanup done.
- `byteplus-faas` postMessage analysis:
  - Downloaded `https://res.gcloudcache.com/bp-fe/byteplus-faas/static/js/1.0.0.128/main.edc16495.js` → `/tmp/faas.js`.
  - Listener lacks origin check but only discovered handler is `go_back`; no sensitive action.
- `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` scan:
  - Top hits are React DOM internals/library code; no actionable sink identified.
- Git/log history checked: prior run was test-only notification, no findings/hints. `result/TEST-NOTIFICATION.md` contents were test-only.
- Confirmed account/session facts:
  - A `/user/basics/` shows profile-completion banner “Continue editing”; account profile verified.
  - B root login and IAM `admin12345` login both work; `testtttt` IAM login did not produce a login request (likely no login profile).
  - IAM user list request exposed `admin12345` AccessKey ID in request notes; test account only.

### Active
- No validated high-impact finding yet.
- Candidate server-side surface still untested: mass assignment on `UpdateProfile` / `CompleteProfile`; exact payload injection not yet proven.
- Candidate SSRF/import surface: `/api/v3/skills/github/import` in `js/a2fa7cdc6775d10e.js` (`ImportGithubSkill`, body `{repo, selected}`, headers `X-Ark-Meta-Account-Id`, `X-Ark-Meta-Project-Name`). Host appears to be Ark BFF/modelark subdomains, which are out of scope; only pursue if reachable through same-origin `console.byteplus.com`.
- Need to persist negative results and endpoint inventory to `result/` per AGENT.md.
- `UpdateUser` 403 behavior is unresolved: both root and admin receive 403; maybe proxy blocks write action, or request format is wrong.

### Blocked
- `rg` unavailable; scans use Python/grep.
- 738MB JS creates heavy library noise; many sink matches are React/echarts/vendor code.
- IAM `UpdateUser` blocked with HTTP 403 regardless of `Method`/field names; mass-assignment proof unavailable through `/api/v2/batch/iam`.
- `testtttt` IAM login failed/no login request; low-privilege IAM identity not available.
- Ark/modelark/arkbff require sibling subdomains that are out of scope.
- No confirmed vulnerability; time budget limited.

## Next Move
1. Checkpoint current negative results, endpoint inventory, and scope notes into `result/` (especially `result/inventory/`, `result/logs/session.md`, and any findings/out-of-scope notes).
2. Systematically enumerate same-origin `/api/top/*` create/update endpoints from `/tmp/bp/crawl_api.txt` and test A/B cross-tenant and mass-assignment candidates with `curl` using `/tmp/cookiehdr.txt`; prioritize account/profile and IAM-adjacent actions.
3. If `/api/v3/skills/github/import` is reachable via `console.byteplus.com` without hitting out-of-scope Ark subdomains, test benign `repo` values for URL-fetch/SSRF behavior; otherwise record as out of scope.
4. Revisit `UpdateProfile`/`CompleteProfile` with captured real UI request bodies and minimal added fields, but only if safe cleanup/reversion is possible.

## Relevant Files
- `skills/AGENT.md`: master workflow/rules; confirmed-vuln format in Section 9.
- `skills/client-side-skill.md`, `skills/server-side-skill.md`: testing methodology.
- `data/targets.txt`: authoritative 85-route scope list.
- `creds/test-account.txt`: A/B test credentials.
- `result/scope.md`: scope interpretation.
- `result/confirmed-vuln.txt`: confirmed findings only; currently empty header.
- `result/logs/session.md`, `result/logs/target-state.txt`, `result/logs/targets.sha256`, `result/logs/login-headers.txt`: session/resume metadata.
- `result/inventory/`, `result/findings/`, `result/client-side/`, `result/server-side/console.byteplus.com/`: output dirs, mostly empty.
- `tools/cdp.mjs`: CDP helper (`cookies`, `eval`, `get <url> [outfile]`).
- `tools/crawl.mjs`: route crawler writing scripts/API JSON per route.
- `/tmp/bp/crawl.json`, `/tmp/bp/crawl_scripts.txt`, `/tmp/bp/crawl_api.txt`: crawl results.
- `/tmp/bp/js/` (2217 files, ~738MB): hashed JS bundles.
- `/tmp/bp/js/68e2d2c26ed70c02.js`: user-mono main bundle (`main.4ec0f485.js`).
- `/tmp/bp/js/94e591e322478cc8.js`, `/tmp/bp/js/b441167ead1eb44e.js`, `/tmp/bp/js/fa1839aa81669f86.js`: `UpdateProfile`/`CompleteProfile` call sites.
- `/tmp/bp/js/a2fa7cdc6775d10e.js`: Ark/AgentKit `ImportGithubSkill` and related APIs.
- `/tmp/faas.js`: downloaded `byteplus-faas` bundle; postMessage `go_back` handler only.
- `/tmp/auth.js`: downloaded `vconsole-auth` bundle; `redirectURI` parsing.
- `/tmp/cookies.json`, `/tmp/cookiehdr.txt`: authenticated A-session cookie material for curl.
- `/tmp/bp/pages/*.html`: raw HTML for all 85 routes.
- `/tmp/bp/scan_sink.txt`, `source_sink.txt`, `msgscan.txt`, `msg_app.txt`, `loc_candidates.txt`, `decode_loc.txt`, `param_nav.txt`: static-analysis dumps.
- `vulnebleti/`: bug-class knowledge notes.
